<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abeid Karume</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1905">1905</a>–<a href="/years/1972">1972</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abeid Karume was leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afro-shirazi-party">Afro-Shirazi Party</a> and became President of Zanzibar after the revolution of January 1964 overthrew the sultan. In April 1964 he agreed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-nyerere">Julius Nyerere</a> to unite Zanzibar with Tanganyika as Tanzania, becoming its first vice-president while ruling Zanzibar autocratically. He was assassinated in 1972.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abeid-karume.jpg" alt="Abeid Karume" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abeid_Karume_1964.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
